{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp2", "text": "Intention is the leader of things; intention is first, they’re made by intention. If with pure intent you speak or act, happiness follows you like a shadow that never leaves.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp2", "chapter": "1. Pairs", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 30, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp6", "text": "When others do not understand, let us, who do understand this, restrain ourselves in this regard; for that is how conflicts are laid to rest.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp6", "chapter": "1. Pairs", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 25, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp11", "text": "Thinking the inessential is essential, seeing the essential as inessential; they don’t realize the essential, for wrong thoughts are their habitat.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp11", "chapter": "1. Pairs", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 21, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp117", "text": "If you do something bad, don’t do it again and again, don’t set your heart on it, for piling up evil is suffering.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp117", "chapter": "9. Wickedness", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 23, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp123", "text": "Avoid wickedness, as a merchant with rich cargo and small escort would avoid a dangerous road, or one who loves life would avoid drinking poison.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp123", "chapter": "9. Wickedness", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 25, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp132", "text": "Creatures love happiness, so if you don’t harm them with a stick in search of your own happiness, after death you will find happiness.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp132", "chapter": "10. The Rod", "tone": "stern", "topics": ["death"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 24, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp133", "text": "Don’t speak harshly, they may speak harshly back. For aggressive speech is painful, and the rod may spring back on you.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp133", "chapter": "10. The Rod", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 21, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp144", "text": "Like a fine horse under the whip, be keen and full of urgency. With faith, ethics, and energy, immersion, and investigation of principles, accomplished in knowledge and conduct, mindful, give up this vast suffering.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp144", "chapter": "10. The Rod", "tone": "stern", "topics": ["generosity", "self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 34, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp151", "text": "Fancy chariots of kings wear out, and even this body gets old. But the truth of the good never gets old— so the good proclaim to the good.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp151", "chapter": "11. Old Age", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 28, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp166", "text": "Never neglect what is good for yourself for the sake of another, however great. Knowing well what is good for yourself, be intent upon your heart’s goal.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp166", "chapter": "12. The Self", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 27, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp167", "text": "Don’t resort to lowly things, don’t abide in negligence, don’t resort to wrong views, don’t perpetuate the world.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp167", "chapter": "13. The World", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 18, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp168", "text": "Get up, don’t be heedless, live by principle, with good conduct. For one of good conduct sleeps at ease, in this world and the next.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp168", "chapter": "13. The World", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 25, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp169", "text": "Live by principle, with good conduct, don’t conduct yourself badly. For one of good conduct sleeps at ease, in this world and the next.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp169", "chapter": "13. The World", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 24, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp210", "text": "Don’t ever get too close to those you like or dislike. For not seeing the liked is suffering, and so is seeing the disliked.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp210", "chapter": "16. The Beloved", "tone": "stern", "topics": [], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 24, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "impatient", "selection": "tone=['stern', 'harsh'] topic=- (curation, not generation)"}
